3-YEAR TOTAL COST OF OWNERSHIP (TCO) & FINANCIAL ANALYSIS
Project: Ace Medicare Clinics Migration to Microsoft Azure

TASKS COMPLETED IN THIS FILE:
1. Modeled a 3-year Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) comparison for 16 physical servers (96 vCPUs, 512 GB RAM, 54 TB storage) using the Microsoft Azure TCO Calculator methodology.
2. Evaluated CapEx (upfront on-premises hardware) vs. OpEx (monthly Azure consumption) across 7 cost categories.
3. Demonstrated the financial impact of Azure Hybrid Benefit and 3-Year Reserved Instances.

====================================================================
1. DETAILED 3-YEAR COST COMPARISON
====================================================================

Category 1: Physical Server and Storage Hardware (CapEx)
- On-Premises (3 Years): $240,000 (Mandatory Year 1 replacement of 16 servers + 50 TB SAN storage)
- Azure Pay-As-You-Go: $0 (Zero physical hardware purchase required)
- Azure Optimized: $0 (Zero physical hardware purchase required)

Category 2: Cloud Compute and Storage Consumption (OpEx)
- On-Premises (3 Years): $0 (Hardware already purchased upfront)
- Azure Pay-As-You-Go: $288,000 ($8,000/month billed at standard on-demand hourly rates)
- Azure Optimized: $158,400 ($4,400/month - 45% savings via 3-Year Reserved Instances and Blob Archive tiering)

Category 3: Windows Server and SQL Enterprise Licensing
- On-Premises (3 Years): $85,000 (Software Assurance and license renewals)
- Azure Pay-As-You-Go: $108,000 (Paying full rental license fees inside standard VM hourly pricing)
- Azure Optimized: $18,000 (83% savings by applying Azure Hybrid Benefit to reuse existing Windows/SQL licenses)

Category 4: Data Center Power and Cooling (HVAC)
- On-Premises (3 Years): $66,000 ($1,833/month for server electricity, backup generators, and 24/7 cooling)
- Azure Pay-As-You-Go: $0 (Included in Microsoft Azure service)
- Azure Optimized: $0 (Included in Microsoft Azure service)

Category 5: IT Administrative and Maintenance Labor
- On-Premises (3 Years): $126,000 ($42,000/year for manual hardware repairs, disk swaps, and OS patching)
- Azure Pay-As-You-Go: $72,000 ($24,000/year - 43% reduction via managed PaaS/SaaS automation)
- Azure Optimized: $72,000 ($24,000/year)

Category 6: Security, HIPAA Compliance, and Backup Services
- On-Premises (3 Years): $33,000 (Local backup media, antivirus, and manual audit preparation)
- Azure Pay-As-You-Go: $45,000 (Microsoft Defender for Cloud HIPAA plan, Azure Key Vault, and Geo-Redundant Backup)
- Azure Optimized: $42,000 (Optimized backup retention lifecycle)

Category 7: One-Time Migration and Security Validation
- On-Premises (3 Years): $0
- Azure Pay-As-You-Go: $47,600 (Year 1 Azure Migrate data replication and HIPAA penetration testing)
- Azure Optimized: $47,600

====================================================================
2. FINAL 3-YEAR TCO SUMMARY
====================================================================
- Total 3-Year On-Premises Cost: $550,000
- Total 3-Year Azure Pay-As-You-Go (Unoptimized): $560,600
- Total 3-Year Azure Optimized Cost: $338,000
- NET 3-YEAR SAVINGS (Azure Optimized vs. On-Premises): $212,000 (38.5% Cost Reduction)

Key Financial Insight:
Simply lifting and shifting 24/7 clinical workloads onto standard Pay-As-You-Go Azure pricing ($560,600) costs $10,600 more than staying on-premises ($550,000). Applying Azure Reserved Instances and Azure Hybrid Benefit is essential to unlock the $212,000 savings.

